 CLÍNICA DE 2012\" encompasses comprehensive recommendations for the treatment and management of various medical conditions. Specifically, it provides guidelines for the treatment of patients with Zollinger-Ellison syndrome and pancreatic tumors. Additionally, the guidelines address the management of patients with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1), detailing when surgical interventions should be considered. Overall, the 2012 Clinical Guidelines serve as a crucial resource for healthcare professionals in the effective treatment of these complex conditions.", "ZOLLINGER-ELLISON SYNDROME:Zollinger-Ellison syndrome is a medical condition characterized by the presence of gastrin-secreting tumors, which result in excessive production of gastric acid. This overproduction can lead to various symptoms, including diarrhea and the development of peptic ulcers. The management of Zollinger-Ellison syndrome often involves surgical intervention, as highlighted in clinical guidelines, emphasizing the importance of addressing the underlying tumors to alleviate the associated symptoms and complications.", "DREIJERINK KM:Dreijerink KM is an author of a referenced study on breast-cancer predisposition in multiple endocrine neoplasia type 1.", "VALDÉS GALLEGO N:Valdés Gallego N is an author of a referenced manual on endocrinology and nutrition.", "GASTRINA:Gastrina is a hormone produced by G cells in the stomach, primarily responsible for stimulating the secretion of gastric acid. It plays a crucial role in the digestive process and is often found to be elevated in patients with gastrinomas, which are tumors that secrete excessive amounts of this hormone. Additionally, gastrin may influence intestinal motility, further contributing to its importance in gastrointestinal function.", "TEST DE SECRETINA:The secretin test is a functional test used to diagnose gastrinomas by measuring the level of gastrin in response to secretin administration.", "HORMONAS GASTROINTESTINALES:HORMONAS GASTROINTESTINALES, or gastrointestinal hormones, are a group of hormones that play a crucial role in regulating various functions within the digestive system. One notable hormone in this category is gastrin, which is particularly significant in the context of gastrinomas, a type of tumor that secretes excessive amounts of gastrin. These hormones are integral to the digestive process, and their levels and functions were evaluated in patients to identify any abnormalities that may affect digestion.", "INHIBIDORES DE LA BOMBA DE PROTONES:Los inhibidores de la bomba de protones son medicamentos que reducen la producción de ácido en el estómago y se utilizan en el tratamiento de diversas condiciones, como el síndrome de Zollinger-Ellison. Estos medicamentos también se han probado en pacientes para tratar la regurgitación. Sin embargo, es importante tener en cuenta que su uso puede estar relacionado con la producción de diarrea.", "GASTRINOMA PANCREÁTICO:Pancreatic gastrinomas are gastrin-secreting tumors that can occur in the pancreas, contributing to the symptoms of Zollinger-Ellison syndrome.", "MIGUEL A. RUBIO HERRERA:Miguel A. Rubio Herrera is a licensed physician and a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition. He currently holds the position of Head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Section at Hospital Clínico San Carlos in Madrid. As a medical professional, he focuses on the fields of endocrinology and nutrition, contributing to the healthcare services at the San Carlos Clinical University Hospital in Madrid.", "UNIVERSIDAD COMPLUTENSE DE MADRID:Universidad Complutense de Madrid is the university where Miguel A. Rubio Herrera completed his doctorate in 1989 and is currently an associate professor.", "SEEDO:SEEDO, or Sociedad Española para el Estudio de la Obesidad, is a prominent organization dedicated to addressing obesity in Spain. It plays a crucial role in establishing therapeutic intervention criteria for obesity and is actively involved in developing consensus guidelines regarding obesity treatment. SEEDO supports the implementation of hypocaloric diets, particularly those based on the Mediterranean diet, recognizing their health benefits in the management of obesity. Through its initiatives, SEEDO aims to promote effective strategies for obesity prevention and treatment, contributing to the overall health of the population.", "NAOS:NAOS is a strategy developed for addressing obesity in Spain, in which Miguel A. Rubio Herrera has participated."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}